```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{amsmath}
\usepackage{amssymb}

\begin{document}

\title{SAT\_O Audit Instructions \\ \large Module: O2 - Emergent Gravitational Action from Filament Ensemble}
\author{}
\date{}
\maketitle

\section*{Audit Testing Instructions}

You are required to audit the module according to the SAT\_O Testing Protocol. The following customized tests must be performed:

\section{Definition Consistency}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Verify that every term (e.g., \( S_{\text{filament}} \), \( g_{\mu\nu} \), \( \ell_f \), \( G_{\text{induced}} \)) is defined exactly as per the SAT\_O Glossary.
    \item \textbf{Action}: List any undefined or non-glossary-matching symbols.
\end{itemize}

\section{Logical Structure Validation}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Trace the logical progression from the single-filament action to the effective gravitational action.
    \item \textbf{Action}: Identify and describe any logical gaps or unsupported transitions.
\end{itemize}

\section{Mathematical Correctness}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Explicitly verify:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Dimensional correctness of major equations: (1), (5), (6), (8).
        \item The heat kernel expansion up to \( O(T) \) order.
        \item The derivation of the induced Newton constant.
    \end{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Action}: Show step-by-step dimensional analysis of \( \Lambda_{\text{induced}} \) and \( G_{\text{induced}} \).
\end{itemize}

\section{Group-Theoretical Integrity}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Not applicable to this module (no gauge group structure).
\end{itemize}

\section{Quantum Consistency Check}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Determine whether loop corrections or effective field theory assumptions could plausibly impact \( G_{\text{induced}} \) and \( \Lambda_{\text{induced}} \).
    \item \textbf{Action}: Discuss whether \( \ell_f \) scale corrections are suppressed.
\end{itemize}

\section{Falsifiability Assessment}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Explicitly identify measurable consequences of the scaling of \( \Lambda_{\text{induced}} \sim \ell_f^{-4} \).
    \item \textbf{Action}: Provide a falsifiability pathway (hypothetical experiment or observation).
\end{itemize}

\section{Independence Verification}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Verify that no external assumptions outside of the SAT\_O2 document and glossary are invoked.
    \item \textbf{Action}: Document any assumptions not defined within the module or glossary.
\end{itemize}

\section{Hidden Parameter Scan}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Scan for free parameters (e.g., \( T \), \( A \)) inserted without derivation.
    \item \textbf{Action}: Identify and list all hidden/unjustified parameters.
\end{itemize}

\section{Failure Mode Analysis}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Hypothesize at least one plausible failure mode.
    \item \textbf{Action}: Write out a failure scenario (e.g., problematic regimes of \( \ell_f \to 0 \) or extreme \( T/A \)).
\end{itemize}

\section*{Explicit Worked Examples}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Dimensional Analysis}:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Verify that \( \Lambda_{\text{induced}} \) has dimensions of \((\text{length})^{-4}\).
        \item Verify that \( G_{\text{induced}} \) corresponds to gravitational coupling dimensions.
    \end{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Falsifiability Example}:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Propose a theoretical or experimental observable tied to \( \ell_f \) or \( G_{\text{induced}} \).
    \end{itemize}
\end{enumerate}

\bigskip

\noindent\textbf{Reminder:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Show all work.
    \item No summary judgments without proof.
    \item No checklist answers --- derive every conclusion step-by-step.
    \item Do not reference external sources --- only use the module and glossary.
\end{itemize}

\end{document}
```

